Build BaraMarket Scanner v2.0: a single-file HTML app that fetches live prediction markets from Polymarket and scores them for capybara relevance, with graceful offline fallback and clear synthetic-data labeling.

## Visual Identity

Display a **Vibybara** logo SVG in the header: a rounded light-brown capybara (#d58d59) with a darker blunt muzzle patch (#704939) running down the front of the face, small dark ears (#220c0d), serene sleepy curved-stroke eyes, soft peachy blush (#e8907a, opacity 0.55), and dark over-ear headphones (#1e0c0b-layered) each with a bright yellow lightning bolt (#ffd23f) on the earcup. The headphones sit atop a thin dark headband arc. Size: 54×54px SVG inline in the header next to the title.

## Domain & Data

Six market interest categories with capybara-relevant keywords:
- **Herd Politics**: election, president, senate, congress, vote, trump, democrat, republican, impeach, parliament, etc.
- **Capycoin & Crypto**: bitcoin, ethereum, crypto, dogecoin, blockchain, token, airdrop, etc.
- **Splash Sports**: nba, nfl, super bowl, world cup, champions league, olympics, etc.
- **Forage Economy**: fed, interest rate, inflation, gdp, recession, tariff, unemployment, stock, cpi, etc.
- **Curious Snout (Sci & Tech)**: openai, spacex, starship, ai, gpt, nasa, nuclear, climate, hurricane, vaccine, etc.
- **Watering Hole Gossip**: oscar, netflix, taylor swift, grammy, box office, emmy, tiktok, spotify, etc.

Anti-keywords that penalize: jaguar, caiman, anaconda, crocodile, animal testing.

## Data Sources

**Live**: Client-side calls to `gamma-api.polymarket.com/events` (limit 75, ordered by 24h volume, active & open markets only). Parse title, tags, market question/description, outcomePrices (YES odds in cents), volume24hr. Timeout: 10s.

**Offline fallback**: 16 bundled synthetic events (2028 election, Bitcoin $150k, Super Bowl LXI, Fed rates, Starship, GPT-6, etc.) clearly marked as fixtures. Used if offline or API fails. Display prominent red warning: "⚠ OFFLINE / SYNTHETIC MODE — the live Polymarket feed could not be reached. Everything below is synthetic sample data..."

## UI (dark theme, monospace)

Header: Vibybara logo + "BARAMARKET SCANNER v2.0" + "scanning live polymarket prediction feeds for capy-relevant action since 2026". Top-right: **source badge** (green "● live · gamma-api.polymarket.com" or red "⚠ synthetic sample data").

Controls: START SCAN / RESCAN button, min-relevance threshold dropdown (30/50/70/90%), search input, JSON/CSV export buttons, progress bar, console log (monospace, scrollable).

Stats grid: feeds scanned, markets crawled, capy matches, top category.

Category filter: 6 toggleable chips, all active by default.

Results: market cards with product tables (market question, matched keywords, category tag, YES odds in cents, 24h volume, relevance %). Score pills: 70%+ green, 45-69% yellow, <45% red. Synthetic markets tagged.

## Core Features

**Fetch engine**: acquireFeeds() tries live gamma-api call first; on failure (network/timeout) or navigator.onLine = false, falls back to SAMPLE_EVENTS. Logs state.

**Scan**: Sequentially process feeds with simulated delays (120–280ms per feed, 40–100ms per market). Score each market. Log progress in real-time.

**Scoring**: Search question+description for keywords, sum weights by category, subtract anti-keyword penalties, clamp 0–100%. Bonus: if score > 0, add Math.min(18, log₁₀(volume+1)×3) for busy markets. Match if ≥threshold AND has a top category.

**Filters**: Results filter by active categories and text search. Update on category chip toggle or search input.

**Source UI**: updateSourceUI() sets sourceBadge and syntheticBanner visibility. Live = green badge + hidden banner. Sample = red badge + visible warning.

**Exports**: JSON (baramarket-scan.json) and CSV (baramarket-scan.csv) include dataSource field ('gamma-api.polymarket.com' or 'synthetic-sample-fixtures') and synthetic boolean flag.

**Empty states**: Before scan: "🔍 no scan data yet — the capybaras are waiting patiently". After scan with no matches: "🙈 no matches under current filters — widen the categories or clear the search".
